msgctxt "100"
msgid "Hello? This is Tabayashi speakin'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "112"
msgid ""
"It's Kiryu. You know the place that's marked on the map you gave me? Well, "
"I found somewhere just like it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "124"
msgid "Y'did!? Well, where is it!?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "136"
msgid "It's in a parking lot in Hatsumachi near the Karaokekan. You can't miss it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "148"
msgid "Okay, hold on. I'll be right there."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "256"
msgid ""
"So... here? Yes, if this is the Kubochi River...\r\n"
"And this is the big street... Then yep! This is the place!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "268"
msgid ""
"Wait a second now... It's all comin' back to me...\r\n"
"Yes, I'm starting to remember where we buried it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "280"
msgid ""
"The treasure oughta be... right behind this parking lot!\r\n"
"Well, I'll go take a look-see. Maybe nobody's dug it up yet."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "340"
msgid ""
"(Could this Yamashita treasure really exist? I guess we're\r\n"
"about to find out...)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "412"
msgid "Well? Did you find anything?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "424"
msgid ""
"I did! There's a vacant lot behind this parking lot.\r\n"
"And I found these buried under a statue out there."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "460"
msgid ""
"These are... a bunch of letters? That's what the Yamashita\r\n"
"treasure is?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "472"
msgid ""
"To be honest... this ain't the Yamashita treasure at all.\r\n"
"They're letters from soldiers to their families that I left\r\n"
"here during the war."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "484"
msgid "What were you doing with a bunch of letters?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "496"
msgid ""
"Well... Y'see... During the war, I was too young and frail to be sent out "
"to the frontlines."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "508"
msgid ""
"Instead, I worked as a postman for the soldiers fighting\r\n"
"here in Okinawa."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "520"
msgid ""
"And the only thing what kept our spirits alive throughout all the death and "
"dyin'... were these letters. Both to and from loving families eagerly "
"awaiting our return."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "532"
msgid ""
"But then the war turned too ugly for us to handle, so we\r\n"
"pulled outta Okinawa and never looked back..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "544"
msgid ""
"...I couldn't bring myself to send these sorrowful letters, written by sons "
"who sacrificed themselves in the war effort. Instead, I buried 'em here and "
"left like a coward."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "556"
msgid ""
"I... I never delivered these soldiers' final words to their families. And "
"the guilt's been hangin' over my head for a long time now..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "568"
msgid "So that's what this is all about..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "580"
msgid ""
"I'm sorry. The whole search for the Yamashita treasure\r\n"
"was a lie. Hope you can find it in your heart to forgive me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "592"
msgid ""
"Don't worry about me. I'm just curious as to what you'll do with those "
"letters now that you have them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "604"
msgid ""
"Hrm... I know a lot of time's gone by, but I'd still like to deliver these "
"to the families of those deceased and gone..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "616"
msgid "Once I do that, I'll finally be able to put the war behind me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "628"
msgid "I see..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "640"
msgid ""
"I'll give you what was buried with the letters. It's old,\r\n"
"but I bet a man like you could still use it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "652"
msgid "You got <Color:8>Antique Chain Mail<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "676"
msgid ""
"Thank you so much, young man. I'll remember your kindness as\r\n"
"long as this old heart keeps thumpin' in my chest... Farewell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "700"
msgid "You got 3,000 EXP."
msgstr ""

